licitly show the biological input data type.\n\nModel interfaces / transformations:\n- The figure compares a classical Horvath epigenetic clock against Qwen3-14B models after SFT and RFT training.\n- Outputs are transformed into predicted age values and evaluated against true age.\n\nFindings:\n- Qwen3-14B RFT has the lowest visible MAE, 4.34 years.\n- Horvath Clock has MAE 4.61 years.\n- Qwen3-14B SFT has the highest MAE, 5.91 years.\n- RFT shows the highest reported R² among the three methods, 0.914."]}, {"figure_index": 3, "page_no": 8, "caption": "Figure 3. Longevity-LLM captures age-dependent signal in proteomic data.", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nThe image is a multi-panel scientific figure labeled **A**, **B**, and **C** comparing predicted versus true age and benchmarking model performance.\n\n**Panel A:** Four scatter plots of **Predicted age, years** versus **True age, years**, each with a dashed diagonal identity line. Points are colored by source: pink for **Chia et al** and cyan for **IoA**. The four methods/models shown are:\n\n- **Kuo Mortality**: MAE = 10.6, R² = 0.028, p = 0.800\n- **Goeminne Chronological**: MAE = 6.7, R² = 0.547, p = 0.937\n- **Goeminne Mortality**: MAE = 6.9, R² = 0.554, p = 0.742\n- **Qwen3-14B SFT**: MAE = 7.9, R² = 0.330, p = 0.713\n\n**Panel B:** Bar chart showing **MAE, years** for the same approaches. Bars are labeled:\n\n- Goeminne chrono: 6.7\n- Goeminne mortality: 6.9\n- Qwen3-14B SFT: 7.9\n- Kuo mortality: 10.6\n\nA red dashed horizontal line labeled **Group mean prediction** is drawn near the top around 10.6 MAE. The Qwen3-14B SFT bar is blue; others are gray.\n\n**Panel C:** Horizontal bar chart comparing model performance by **Jaccard Index**. **Qwen3-14B SFT** has the highest value, labeled **0.0718**, followed by models including **grok-3**, **grok-4**, **o3**, **gpt-5**, **gpt-4.1**, **gpt-5.2**, **claude-sonnet-4-5**, **gpt-4.1-mini**, **o4-mini**, and several Gemini/DeepSeek models. The x-axis is 